iteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"objective\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_turns\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"loop-until-done\",\n      \"description\": \"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_iterations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_scoring\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_repeats\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"open-claude-design\",\n      \"description\": \"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"discover_references\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ralph\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_loops\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tournament\",\n      \"description\": \"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_attempts\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"n_evaluations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"pivots\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"seed\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"models\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"action":"list","items":[{"name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.","inputs":[{"name":"task","required":true},{"name":"verifier_count","required":false},{"name":"max_repairs","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"accept_mean","required":false},{"name":"reask_limit","required":false}]},{"name":"classify-and-act","description":"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"categories","required":false},{"name":"confidence_threshold","required":false}]},{"name":"fan-out-and-synthesize","description":"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_branches","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"generate-and-filter","description":"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_candidates","required":false},{"name":"shortlist_size","required":false},{"name":"use_judge","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"goal","description":"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"objective","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_turns","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"loop-until-done","description":"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_iterations","required":false},{"name":"progress_scoring","required":false},{"name":"progress_repeats","required":false}]},{"name":"open-claude-design","description":"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"discover_references","required":false}]},{"name":"ralph","description":"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_loops","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"tournament","description":"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_attempts","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false},{"name":"n_evaluations","required":false},{"name":"pivots","required":false},{"name":"seed","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"models","required":false}]}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788147147530}]}
