{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning fan-out synthesis for architecture extraction**\n\n**Launching fan-out for repo inspection**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cc3b2087d2baa370eeb27064a4\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning fan-out synthesis for architecture extraction**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Launching fan-out for repo inspection**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Architecture pass: use `fan-out-and-synthesize` with independent branches for (1) module/entry-point mapping, (2) runtime/data-flow and storage tracing, and (3) README-vs-code discrepancy and risk review, then synthesize at a barrier. This covers repository uncertainty and cross-checks claims before I write the five required artifacts. The graph is acyclic: branches → synthesis; no repair loop is needed because I will validate JSON/CSV structure deterministically afterward. Model stages use the workflow’s configured role policy (mapping/synthesis high, review high); deterministic validation stays local.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cf431487d28aedf3529112e4e4\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2xZfUdkpvvEXcuSfjV6vX5UE|fc_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5d1797087d2a2f3abd025b11ebd","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"run","workflow":"fan-out-and-synthesize","inputs":{"prompt":"<keepContext>Inspect only /workspace/in/repo; do not modify it and do not use internet. Produce an evidence-backed repository architecture map for these required deliverables: module_map.json with modules, canonical entry_points including minisvc.cli:main and minisvc.api.routes:register_routes, dependency edges (imports/calls/instantiates/reads_config/persists_to), key functions, and CLI startup plus HTTP create-order runtime flows; architec