{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning fan-out synthesis for architecture extraction**\n\n**Launching fan-out for repo inspection**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cc3b2087d2baa370eeb27064a4\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning fan-out synthesis for architecture extraction**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Launching fan-out for repo inspection**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Architecture pass: use `fan-out-and-synthesize` with independent branches for (1) module/entry-point mapping, (2) runtime/data-flow and storage tracing, and (3) README-vs-code discrepancy and risk review, then synthesize at a barrier. This covers repository uncertainty and cross-checks claims before I write the five required artifacts. The graph is acyclic: branches → synthesis; no repair loop is needed because I will validate JSON/CSV structure deterministically afterward. Model stages use the workflow’s configured role policy (mapping/synthesis high, review high); deterministic validation stays local.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cf431487d28aedf3529112e4e4\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2xZfUdkpvvEXcuSfjV6vX5UE|fc_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5d1797087d2a2f3abd025b11ebd","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"run","workflow":"fan-out-and-synthesize","inputs":{"prompt":"<keepContext>Inspect only /workspace/in/repo; do not modify it and do not use internet. Produce an evidence-backed repository architecture map for these required deliverables: module_map.json with modules, canonical entry_points including minisvc.cli:main and minisvc.api.routes:register_routes, dependency edges (imports/calls/instantiates/reads_config/persists_to), key functions, and CLI startup plus HTTP create-order runtime flows; architecture.md; doc_code_discrepancies.csv covering readonly enforcement, retry behavior, audit persistence; risk_register.csv covering storage durability, audit behavior, config/runtime environment, API validation; onboarding_plan.md. Cite concrete filenames/functions and distinguish package marker files (__init__.py) from active business logic. Compare README/design notes to actual code. Return structured, detailed findings for a synthesis writer.</keepContext>","max_branches":3,"max_concurrency":3}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2400,"output":496,"cacheRead":13824,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":154,"totalTokens":16720,"cost":{"input":0.00048000000000000007,"output":0.0005951999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00027648,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00135168}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788147147531,"responseId":"resp_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cbc9cc87d29034b568339301e7","rawStopReason":"completed"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2xZfUdkpvvEXcuSfjV6vX5UE|fc_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5d1797087d2a2f3abd025b11ebd","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"run\",\n  \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n  \"runId\": \"3b10269b-ed7a-4cb4-8d7b-ca345a555e77\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"result\": \"Output saved to: /workspace/.atomic/workflows/runs/fan-out-and-synthesize-edef5132-bbdd-45a8-9ed7-cb9aeff9cf1f/synthesis.md (19.1 KB, 326 lines). Read this file if needed.\\nTranscript saved to: /home/highlander/runtime/.atomic/workflows/runs/3b10269b-ed7a-4cb4-8d7b-ca345a555e77/transcripts/96b1e6ad38fbee06-synthesis.md.transcript.md (62.0 KB, 942 lines). Search it with rg, read narrow line ranges, and do not read it whole.\",\n    \"partitions\": [\n      \"Code architecture and runtime flows\",\n      \"Docs versus code discrepancies\",\n      \"Risks and onboarding synthesis inputs\"\n    ],\n    \"branch_artifact_paths\": [\n      \"/workspace/.a