apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"task\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"verifier_count\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_repairs\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"accept_mean\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"reask_limit\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"classify-and-act\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"categories\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"confidence_threshold\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n      \"description\": \"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_branches\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"generate-and-filter\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_candidates\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"shortlist_size\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"use_judge\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"goal\",\n      \"description\": \"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"objective\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_turns\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"loop-until-done\",\n      \"description\": \"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_iterations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_scoring\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_repeats\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"open-claude-design\",\n      \"description\": \"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"discover_references\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ralph\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_loops\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tournament\",\n      \"description\": \"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_attempts\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"n_evaluations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"pivots\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"seed\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"models\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"action":"list","items":[{"name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.","inputs":[{"name":"task","required":true},{"name":"verifier_count","required":false},{"name":"max_repairs","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"accept_mean","required":false},{"name":"reask_limit","required":false}]},{"name":"classify-and-act","description":"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"categories","required":false},{"name":"confidence_threshold","required":false}]},{"name":"fan-out-and-synthesize","description":"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_branches","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"generate-and-filter","description":"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_candidates","required":false},{"name":"shortlist_size","required":false},{"name":"use_judge","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"goal","description":"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"objective","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_turns","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"loop-until-done","description":"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_iterations","required":false},{"name":"progress_scoring","required":false},{"name":"progress_repeats","required":false}]},{"name":"open-claude-design","description":"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"discover_references","required":false}]},{"name":"ralph","description":"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_loops","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"tournament","description":"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_attempts","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false},{"name":"n_evaluations","required":false},{"name":"pivots","required":false},{"name":"seed","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"models","required":false}]}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788147147530},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning fan-out synthesis for architecture extraction**\n\n**Launching fan-out for repo inspection**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cc3b2087d2baa370eeb27064a4\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning fan-out synthesis for architecture extraction**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Launching fan-out for repo inspection**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Architecture pass: use `fan-out-and-synthesize` with independent branches for (1) module/entry-point mapping, (2) runtime/data-flow and storage tracing, and (3) README-vs-code discrepancy and risk review, then synthesize at a barrier. This covers repository uncertainty and cross-checks claims before I write the five required artifacts. The graph is acyclic: branches → synthesis; no repair loop is needed because I will validate JSON/CSV structure deterministically afterward. Model stages use the workflow’s configured role policy (mapping/synthesis high, review high); deterministic validation stays local.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cf431487d28aedf3529112e4e4\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2xZfUdkpvvEXcuSfjV6vX5UE|fc_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5d1797087d2a2f3abd025b11ebd","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"run","workflow":"fan-out-and-synthesize","inputs":{"prompt":"<keepContext>Inspect only /workspace/in/repo; do not modify it and do not use internet. Produce an evidence-backed repository architecture map for these required deliverables: module_map.json with modules, canonical entry_points including minisvc.cli:main and minisvc.api.routes:register_routes, dependency edges (imports/calls/instantiates/reads_config/persists_to), key functions, and CLI startup plus HTTP create-order runtime flows; architecture.md; doc_code_discrepancies.csv covering readonly enforcement, retry behavior, audit persistence; risk_register.csv covering storage durability, audit behavior, config/runtime environment, API validation; onboarding_plan.md. Cite concrete filenames/functions and distinguish package marker files (__init__.py) from active business logic. Compare README/design notes to actual code. Return structured, detailed findings for a synthesis writer.</keepContext>","max_branches":3,"max_concurrency":3}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2400,"output":496,"cacheRead":13824,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":154,"totalTokens":16720,"cost":{"input":0.00048000000000000007,"output":0.0005951999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00027648,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00135168}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788147147531,"responseId":"resp_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5cbc9cc87d29034b568339301e7","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2xZfUdkpvvEXcuSfjV6vX5UE|fc_04b379b479ca7a98016a94f5d1797087d2a2f3abd025b11ebd","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"run\",\n  \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n  \"runId\": \"3b10269b-ed7a-4cb4-8d7b-ca345a555e77\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"result\": \"Output saved to: /workspace/.atomic/workflows/runs/fan-out-and-synthesize-edef5132-bbdd-45a8-9ed7-cb9aeff9cf1f/synthesis.md (19.1 KB, 326 lines). Read this file if needed.\\nTranscript saved to: /home/highlander/runtime/.atomic/workflows/runs/3b10269b-ed7a-4cb4-8d7b-ca345a555e77/transcripts/96b1e6ad38fbee06-synthesis.md.transcript.md (62.0 KB, 942 lines). Search it with rg, read narrow line ranges, and do not read it whole.\",\n    \"partitions\": [\n      \"Code architecture and runtime flows\",\n      \"Docs versus code discrepancies\",\n      \"Risks and onboarding synthesis inputs\"\n    ],\n    \"branch_artifact_paths\": [\n      \"/workspace/.atomic/workflows/runs/fan-out-and-synthesize-edef5132-bbdd-45a8-9ed7-cb9aeff9cf1f/branch-01-code-architecture-and-runtime-flows.md\",\n      \"/workspace/.atomic/workflows/runs/fan-out-and-synthesize-edef5132-bbdd-45a8-9ed7-cb9aeff9cf1f/branch-02-docs-versus-code-discrepancies.md\",\n      \"/workspace/.atomic/workflows/runs/fan-out-and-synthesize-edef5132-bbdd-45a8-9ed7-cb9aeff9cf1f/branch-03-risks-and-onboarding-synthesis-inputs.md\"\n    ],\n    \"synthesis_path\": \